From 539d70de79ea3aec0724de2f05ba03d381259495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Peripheral Pretender setup <pp-setup@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 18:20:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: Quectel L86 GNSS module, the GNSS Click

A chardev on the socket's UART, 9600 baud paced at the baud rate: the
L86's boot lines, NMEA 4.10 sentences in its order and talkers with and
without a fix, PMTK220/251/314/161/101-104 with their acknowledgements,
RESET on RST. Position, altitude, satellites (below 4: no fix), speed
and course are QOM properties; date and time come from the RTC.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst |  13 +
 hw/misc/meson.build                   |   1 +
 hw/misc/mikrobus.c                    |   8 +
 hw/misc/quectel_l86.c                 | 595 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/hw/misc/quectel_l86.h         |  18 +
 5 files changed, 635 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 hw/misc/quectel_l86.c
 create mode 100644 include/hw/misc/quectel_l86.h

diff --git a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
index 1d4c059..4a544d6 100644
--- a/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
+++ b/docs/system/arm/pic32cm-mc00-cpro.rst
@@ -142,6 +142,19 @@ headers, so one UART Click at a time; it then takes SERCOM3's place in
   (``click-pot``). QOM property ``position`` (per mille of the travel,
   500 at start); ``top-mv`` is 3300 for OUT SEL on 3V3.
 
+``gnss``
+  GNSS Click (v100): a Quectel L86 GNSS module on the UART
+  (``chardev-quectel-l86``), 9600 baud, paced at the baud rate. It sends
+  the boot lines ($PMTK011, $PMTK010,001/002), then NMEA sentences once per
+  fix interval in the module's order and talkers (GNRMC, GPVTG, GPGGA,
+  GNGSA, GPGSV, GLGSV, GNGLL, GPTXT; all GP without a fix, the clock then
+  counting from 1980-01-05 23:59:42), and answers PMTK220, 251, 314, 161
+  and 101-104. RESET on RST (active low), FORCE_ON on CS (R4 10 kOhm
+  pull-up; backup mode not modelled). QOM properties ``lat-udeg``,
+  ``lon-udeg``, ``alt-dm``, ``satellites`` (below 4: no fix), ``fix``,
+  ``speed-ckn``, ``course-cdeg``; the date and time come from the RTC
+  (``-rtc``).
+
 SPI Clicks on both headers share the SPI bus; each listens only while its
 own CS is low (or, for the 74HC595 and MAX7219, latches on its own CS).
 
